Chromatique modifications, made in October 2026, replace static evaluation with
the project's own trained network, add a learned move-ordering policy, preserve
the raw en-passant/repetition feature contract, and prohibit Stockfish NNUE
evaluation. Standalone release packaging on 2026-10-19 adds v4 identification
and executable-relative model discovery. Search and evaluation mathematics are
unchanged by that packaging. Modified files are listed in release.json and the
complete diff against the pinned upstream is in docs/stockfish-changes.patch.

The complete corresponding engine source, build system, model in editable JSON
and native format, and original copyright/license notices are distributed here.
The stock Stockfish NNUE network and any external game/puzzle datasets are not
included. The default bundled model is Chromatique's retained v4 outcome-learning
pilot; the original pure-v4 model is retained separately. Both are Chromatique's
own fully learned networks and are distributed under the same license.

The 2026-10-27 model update changes trained policy/value parameters only. It does
not modify the C++ search, feature definitions, neural inference, or architecture.

The src/incbin helper retains its upstream UNLICENCE.
